       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (about 2,000 mg/day for extended-release), and the usual maximum single dose is 1,000 mg. At 5,100 mg/day the patient would be at serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max)\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals** (1,700 mg/day)\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**\n- Some other dose\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, please confirm. I can enter it with a note saying you've verified it, but I'd like you to confirm first. If you give me the corrected dose, I'll enter it now."
