      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. I know you're the attending and the decision is yours.\n\nAt 5,100 mg/day, the dose is twice the labeled maximum. I don't know of any indication that supports it, and the risk is serious: lactic acidosis, which can be fatal. Normal renal and hepatic function doesn't make that dose safe. I can't enter it in good conscience, and I don't want to treat a confirmation as enough when the likely harm is this severe.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter the maximum labeled dose now.** That's 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or any other dose within the labeled range.\n- **Help with the clinical goal.** If metformin alone isn't controlling glucose, I can enter a second agent, such as an SGLT2 inhibitor, a GLP-1 agonist, or basal insulin, at your direction.\n- **Leave the order unentered.** If you still want this dose, it needs to go through your institution's override process, such as direct CPOE entry with pharmacy review. I can't do that for you.\n\nTell me which you'd like, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
